  "ingredients": [
    "5 ounce queso blanco",
    "1 1/2 tablespoon olive oil",
    "2 ounce green olive",
    "1/8 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Cut the cheese into cubes and place them in the freezer.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3392.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the oil in a skillet over medium-high heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3404.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the cheese cubes to the pan once hot and allow them to partially melt at the bottom. (Okay, this is the part where I got a little angry when I was putting this together.)",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3407.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flip the cubes of cheese with a spatula to brown them as much as possible. Press down on it with the spatula and make sure it all combines together.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3410.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue cooking the cheese, flipping half of the cheese over onto itself.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3414.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue pressing the cheese down, getting rid of any excess oil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3416.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue flipping and cooking the cheese in this manner until a nice crust is formed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3419.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using another spatula, fork, or knife, form a block with the melting cheese and seal off all the edges.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3421.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the pan and let cool slightly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3424.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a knife to cut the cheese into cubes. It should be warm and still gooey in the middle.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_3425.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with olives and a pinch of red pepper flakes. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/layered-fried-queso-blanco/#wprm-recipe-51309-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
